## Problem 6 — the symptom

Edit `ex6/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface LoopHealth {
  meanDelayMs: number;
  p99DelayMs: number;
  maxDelayMs: number;
  utilization: number;                       // 0..1
  verdict: "healthy" | "saturated" | "blocked" | "idle-but-slow";
}

export function measureLoopHealth(
  work: () => void | Promise<void>,
  options?: { resolutionMs?: number; p99WarnMs?: number },
): Promise<LoopHealth>
```

Enable a `monitorEventLoopDelay` histogram and take an
`eventLoopUtilization()` baseline, run `work`, then read both. Convert the
histogram's nanoseconds to milliseconds.

Verdicts:

- `"blocked"` when `maxDelayMs >= 10 * p99DelayMs` and `maxDelayMs >= 50` —
  one long synchronous stall rather than steady pressure;
- `"saturated"` when `utilization >= 0.8` and `p99DelayMs >= p99WarnMs`
  (default 50);
- `"idle-but-slow"` when `utilization < 0.4` and `p99DelayMs >= p99WarnMs` —
  the loop is not busy, so the delay came from somewhere else;
- `"healthy"` otherwise.

Disable the histogram before returning.

